WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.934
Fox News has reportedly been
gripped by paranoia and fear

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:07.367
as on-air personalities worry
they could be next to go

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:09.734
after last week's surprise
ouster of Tucker Carlson.

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:12.767
Meanwhile, President Biden
joked about a possible rematch

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:14.300
with Donald Trump in 2024

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.834
as Trump's likely main rival
for the GOP nomination,

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:18.300
Ron DeSantis, loses steam.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.534
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:22.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:25.934
The conservative movement

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:28.133
is in a state of panic
and disarray right now

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.334
after a string of electoral
and legal defeats.

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:31.834
Their front-runner
for the nomination

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:34.200
is currently under indictment
and facing more investigations.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.634
They keep losing big races
in key swing states,

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:38.567
from the 2022 Senate races

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.634
to the Wisconsin Supreme Court
election in April.

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:42.968
And now their leading
propaganda network

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:45.801
has been forced to pay out
a massive defamation settlement

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:48.000
and cut ties
with their top-rated host,

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.367
Tucker Carlson, seen here
recording a hostage video

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:52.767
from the inside
of a Bass Pro Shop.

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:55.067
And that sense of panic and fear

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:57.968
has apparently set in
at Fox News itself.

00:00:57.968 --> 00:00:59.234
"Rolling Stone" reported the...

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.434
Oh, my God,
fake names is so much fun.

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:15.501
"Oh, sorry.
Got to take this.

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:19.033
It's my Aunt Joan, as you can
all see from the caller ID.

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:20.167
Hi, Joan.
What's that?

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:21.400
You need to have
a tooth extracted?

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.834
Oh, my God, that's terrible.

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:24.467
You know what else is terrible
and about to get extracted?

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:27.567
Tucker Carlson. Okay.
Got to go. I love you, Joan.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:29.467
And just like this
and every conversation,

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:30.901
this is off the record."

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:31.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:32.968
Of course, knowing their hosts,

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:34.634
I'm guessing some of their names
are much dumber.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.701
Like, Brian Kilmeade
definitely has a reporter

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:38.434
listed in his phone
as Santa Claus,

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:41.534
although that definitely
will backfire on him.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:42.634
When that person calls,

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:44.167
he's gonna think
it's actually Santa Claus.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.567
"Oh, my God, good.
You got my letter. Okay.

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:47.467
I want to change
the PlayStation to an Xbox.

00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:50.000
And also, I'm not
into Funko Pops anymore."

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.100
The sense of panic at Fox
is apparently so intense

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:55.100
that other hosts who pushed the
big lie about the 2020 election

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.767
are worried they could
also get fired.

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:04.267
Oh, my God,
it's like a horror movie,

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:05.701
except in this movie,

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:08.133
the ax murderer is
a 92-year-old Australian man,

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:10.300
and instead
of chasing his victims,

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.734
he just makes them come to him.

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:14.801
"Pick up some speed and run
to this chainsaw, you [bleep]"

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:19.767
Also, we'll know when
Jeanine Pirro gets fired

00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:21.701
because it'll get so quiet.

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:23.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:25.868
We're right across the street
from the Fox News headquarters,

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:28.133
and we can hear her screaming
whenever she's on the air.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:30.234
Here, I'll show you.
Open the window.

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:32.734
-You presented him
with your fake dossier

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:34.734
alleging the president
had prostitutes

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.934
peeing on him in Moscow.

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.934
And it's possible...
-Close it.

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:41.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:42.467
One thing is clear,

00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:44.267
Fox definitely seems like
an insane place to work.

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:45.801
As we told you last week,

00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:48.901
Fox reportedly has a dossier of
alleged dirt on Tucker Carlson,

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.300
and he's not the only one.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:53.100
They reportedly do it to all
their on-air personalities.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.434
One ex-Fox News anchor
lamented...

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:05.334
And another departed
Fox News host added...

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:07.901
That's insane.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.734
They keep files full
of damaging information

00:03:09.734 --> 00:03:11.968
so they can use it
against you later as blackmail.

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:13.801
Not only does NBC
not have a file on me,

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:15.167
they don't even know
what I do here.

00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:18.701
Like, the other day, I saw
an executive in the hallway,

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:21.234
and they said, "Hey, 'Weekend
Update' was great on Saturday."

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.467
And I said, "Thanks,
but I have my own show now."

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:24.467
And they said, "You do?

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:25.834
Well, we're sorry
to see you go."

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:30.467
And I was like,
"No, it's on -- it's on NBC."

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:31.534
And they said, "What time?"

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:33.200
And I said,
"12:37 in the morning."

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.167
And then they laughed
like that was a joke.

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:37.601
But it's not a joke time.

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:39.701
It's a real time.

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:43.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.634
I didn't pick it, alright?

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:47.634
It wasn't like, "Oh, no,
I want a seven in there."

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:53.300
Anyway, the sense
of panic and fear

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.434
over at the right's
leading propaganda network

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.467
is emblematic of where
the MAGA movement

00:03:57.467 --> 00:03:59.334
is right now, broadly speaking.

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:01.400
Just look at
Florida governor Ron DeSantis,

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.767
who's been sinking in the polls

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:04.167
after starting out
with a lot of hype.

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:06.167
Look how nervous and shaky he is

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:07.634
now that he's hit
some roadblocks

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:09.234
and has come under fire
from Donald Trump.

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:10.767
-What will Ron DeSantis do?

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:13.567
He is trailing in the polls,
struggling with endorsements.

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.968
And Trump clearly smells blood.

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:17.634
-According to a new
"Wall Street Journal" poll

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:21.234
taken last week, Trump pulled in
48% of the support

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:23.534
among likely
Republican primary voters.

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:25.767
The next person closest
to him is DeSantis,

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:28.734
who is 24 points behind.

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:34.634
-I'm not -- I'm not a candidate.

00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:37.901
So we'll see if
and when that changes.

00:04:37.901 --> 00:04:40.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:44.767
-You guys know the last hole
on a mini-golf course over here.

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:46.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:48.634
I mean, that's one question.
He answered one question.

00:04:48.634 --> 00:04:52.000
And he looks like he's plunging
400 feet on a roller coaster.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:55.367
DeSantis is getting nervous

00:04:55.367 --> 00:04:57.467
because Trump has been
attacking him relentlessly,

00:04:57.467 --> 00:04:59.300
both in public
and behind the scenes.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.834
For example, Trump's campaign

00:05:00.834 --> 00:05:02.534
orchestrated a series
of endorsements

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:04.300
from GOP members of Congress

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.133
from DeSantis'
home state of Florida

00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:08.467
specifically
to embarrass DeSantis

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.100
and get inside his head.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.000
Trump's aides have
reportedly mocked...

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:35.834
And if anyone's capable of a
mind[bleep] it's Donald Trump.

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:37.934
I mean, back in 2016,

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:40.000
Lindsey Graham said
that if they nominated Trump,

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.567
the Republican Party
would be destroyed

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:42.634
and they would deserve it.

00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:44.400
And now he's on TV
crying and begging

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.501
for supporters to send money
to Trump's legal fund.

00:05:46.501 --> 00:05:49.634
He probably has no memory
of what happened in between.

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:52.467
His body's covered in Sharpie
like the guy from "Memento."

00:05:52.467 --> 00:05:53.868
[ As Graham ]
"He's mind[bleep] you."

00:05:53.868 --> 00:05:55.534
What the hell?

00:05:55.534 --> 00:06:00.100
Mee-maw, have you been writing
on me in your sleep again?

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:04.400
Told you to break
the Ambiens in half, you witch.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:05.567
[ Normal voice ]
DeSantis is getting shaky

00:06:05.567 --> 00:06:07.400
because the hype
is giving way to reality

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.868
as election season gets closer.

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.234
I mean, I can't believe
I'm saying this,

00:06:10.234 --> 00:06:12.167
but the 2024
presidential election

00:06:12.167 --> 00:06:14.200
is already ramping up,
which is insane.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.901
I can't stand how early
these things start now.

00:06:16.901 --> 00:06:18.934
The other day, my 5-year-old
came home from school

00:06:18.934 --> 00:06:22.868
and told me he launched an
exploratory committee for 2076.

00:06:22.868 --> 00:06:24.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.234 --> 00:06:25.968
Then I asked him
if he has a super PAC,

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:27.968
and he told me,
"No, that's just a backpack."

00:06:27.968 --> 00:06:31.567
And that is today's
"Politics Jokes for Kids."

00:06:31.567 --> 00:06:32.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.901 --> 00:06:34.033
See?

00:06:34.033 --> 00:06:36.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:38.234 --> 00:06:40.300
Kids can watch
"A Closer Look," too.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.200
Anyway, enough of that
[bleep] bull[bleep]

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.868
I'm sorry, sorry.
Kids are watching.

00:06:44.868 --> 00:06:46.734
Enough of that [bleep] nonsense.

00:06:46.734 --> 00:06:50.434
Now, obviously, we're still
a year and a half away,

00:06:50.434 --> 00:06:52.434
so a lot could change,
like, I don't know,

00:06:52.434 --> 00:06:54.133
the Republican nominee
could be running

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:55.667
while under house arrest.

00:06:55.667 --> 00:06:58.734
[ As Trump ] Sleepy Joe has been
a disaster for this country.

00:06:58.734 --> 00:07:00.701
[ Beeping ]
Sorry.

00:07:00.701 --> 00:07:03.934
That's my ankle monitor.

00:07:03.934 --> 00:07:05.501
My ankle monitor is very smart

00:07:05.501 --> 00:07:06.934
and knows
whenever I leave my house,

00:07:06.934 --> 00:07:09.334
which means my probation officer
will be here shortly

00:07:09.334 --> 00:07:10.334
to escort me back home.

00:07:10.334 --> 00:07:12.200
Probation?

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:15.167
We love probation,
don't we, folks?

00:07:15.167 --> 00:07:16.334
One of the best "bations."

00:07:16.334 --> 00:07:20.234
It means you're a pro at bation.

00:07:20.234 --> 00:07:22.234
And, of course,
the only level above pro

00:07:22.234 --> 00:07:24.000
when it comes to bation
is master.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.367
[ Normal voice ] And that's...

00:07:26.367 --> 00:07:29.534
that's a politics joke
for 12-year-olds.

00:07:29.534 --> 00:07:32.300
[ Laughter ]
NBC has asked --

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:34.067 --> 00:07:37.834
NBC has asked us to hit
all the major demographics.

00:07:37.834 --> 00:07:39.934
So anyway, a lot can change.

00:07:39.934 --> 00:07:43.367
But as of right now, the likely
matchup we're looking at

00:07:43.367 --> 00:07:46.100
is a rematch between
Joe Biden and Donald Trump.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:48.834
And voters really
don't seem to want that.

00:07:48.834 --> 00:07:52.200
-Americans are not excited
about the prospect

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.567
of a Joe Biden/Donald Trump
rematch.

00:07:54.567 --> 00:07:56.334
-This is a rematch nobody wants.

00:07:56.334 --> 00:07:59.000
-There is very little appetite
on either side

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.734
of the political spectrum
for a rematch here.

00:08:01.734 --> 00:08:04.634
And as you see there,
70% do not believe

00:08:04.634 --> 00:08:06.701
that Joe Biden should run
for president again,

00:08:06.701 --> 00:08:10.501
and 60% believe
Donald Trump should not either.

00:08:10.501 --> 00:08:12.133
-At this point,
the Biden/Trump rematch

00:08:12.133 --> 00:08:14.634
just feels like your six-month
checkup at the dentist.

00:08:14.634 --> 00:08:16.834
Like, when they ask you
when you want to come back,

00:08:16.834 --> 00:08:18.033
you want to say, "Never."

00:08:18.033 --> 00:08:19.901
But, you know,
you just have to pick

00:08:19.901 --> 00:08:22.801
a random Tuesday in November
and get it over with.

00:08:22.801 --> 00:08:25.167
You guys remember how thrilling
the 2008 election was?

00:08:25.167 --> 00:08:27.067
Hundreds of thousands of people
pouring into the streets

00:08:27.067 --> 00:08:29.000
across the country, hugging
and celebrating all night.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.167
2008 was like a coked-up
midnight rave

00:08:31.167 --> 00:08:34.234
in a Brooklyn warehouse
compared to 2024.

00:08:34.234 --> 00:08:35.634
A Biden-versus-Trump rematch

00:08:35.634 --> 00:08:38.000
is like a book club
you feel obligated to attend,

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:41.133
even though everyone there
annoys the [bleep] out of you.

00:08:41.133 --> 00:08:43.634
"No, Jessica,
I did not read the book.

00:08:43.634 --> 00:08:45.834
No one read the book.
I'm here for the wine.

00:08:45.834 --> 00:08:47.133
And if you got
a problem with that,

00:08:47.133 --> 00:08:50.300
you can go eat, pray,
and [bleep] yourself."

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:52.133
[ Laughter ]

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:58.467
"I read the cover, Jessica."

00:09:00.334 --> 00:09:01.601
Even Biden's announcement

00:09:01.601 --> 00:09:03.133
that he was running
for re-election was sedated.

00:09:03.133 --> 00:09:04.868
It was just a video message
he posted

00:09:04.868 --> 00:09:07.434
on the four-year anniversary
of his first presidential bid.

00:09:07.434 --> 00:09:09.434
Over the weekend, Biden joked
about that announcement

00:09:09.434 --> 00:09:11.100
at the annual White House
Correspondents' Dinner.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:13.701
-I just announced
my re-election campaign.

00:09:13.701 --> 00:09:16.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:16.334 --> 00:09:17.767
Some of you --

00:09:19.767 --> 00:09:23.868
Some of you scooped that I'd
announced it in the video.

00:09:23.868 --> 00:09:25.701
But really, you really
all thought in your heart

00:09:25.701 --> 00:09:27.767
that I just blurted it out,
didn't you?

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:28.801
[ Laughter ]

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:30.267
-I mean, yeah, of course we did.

00:09:30.267 --> 00:09:32.901
I just assumed that's how we'll
find out if aliens are real.

00:09:32.901 --> 00:09:34.133
[ As Biden ]
Look, here's the deal, Jack.

00:09:34.133 --> 00:09:35.667
When I was a kid
growing up in Scranton,

00:09:35.667 --> 00:09:38.067
I didn't have money for the bus,
so I rode a bike.

00:09:38.067 --> 00:09:39.634
Just like E.T. was real,
by the way.

00:09:39.634 --> 00:09:42.234
I met him.

00:09:42.234 --> 00:09:44.501
Just met -- Just met E.T.
at Area 51,

00:09:44.501 --> 00:09:46.467
took him for a joyride
in my Stingray.

00:09:46.467 --> 00:09:48.667
[ Laughter ]

00:09:48.667 --> 00:09:51.100
He just phoned home
and he told them it was rad.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:53.200
[ Laughter ]

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:55.767
[ Normal voice ] But, yes, Biden
did announce his re-election bid

00:09:55.767 --> 00:09:57.100
in a video message last week

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:59.100
as opposed to a live address,
which was a good call.

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:00.834
That way if he wandered off
at the end,

00:10:00.834 --> 00:10:03.467
they could just edit
that part out.

00:10:03.467 --> 00:10:06.133
Look, we're never gonna stop
using that video.

00:10:06.133 --> 00:10:07.400
And you know why?

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:10.200
Because Republicans
give us new content nonstop.

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:12.868
But for Biden,
that's pretty much it.

00:10:12.868 --> 00:10:14.901
Well, that and the stair thing.

00:10:14.901 --> 00:10:16.968
[ Laughter ]

00:10:16.968 --> 00:10:18.801
As we mentioned,
Biden released that video

00:10:18.801 --> 00:10:20.534
on the four-year anniversary
of his first campaign launch,

00:10:20.534 --> 00:10:21.601
which is crazy to me.

00:10:21.601 --> 00:10:23.033
I can't believe
it's been four years

00:10:23.033 --> 00:10:24.734
since Biden first announced
he was running for president.

00:10:24.734 --> 00:10:26.300
Since then,
we've had a pandemic,

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:28.367
an economic meltdown,
a coup attempt.

00:10:28.367 --> 00:10:30.501
It doesn't feel like four years.
It feels like 40 years.

00:10:30.501 --> 00:10:32.334
I mean, when was Trump's
first announcement?

00:10:32.334 --> 00:10:35.801
1912? Was it in black-and-white
newsreel footage?

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:38.133
[ Announcer voice ]
Here he comes, boys,
the mammoth of Midtown,

00:10:38.133 --> 00:10:40.767
the behemoth of business,
the Colossus of crime,

00:10:40.767 --> 00:10:42.267
Mr. Donald J. Trump himself.

00:10:42.267 --> 00:10:44.400
Look at him waving as he rides
down the escalator

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:45.868
from the Trump Tower food court.

00:10:45.868 --> 00:10:47.868
Give 'em hell, Donald.

00:10:47.868 --> 00:10:50.367
[ Normal voice ] And that's
a joke for old people.

00:10:50.367 --> 00:10:51.701
[ Laughter ]

00:10:51.701 --> 00:10:54.701
We did it. We did it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:54.701 --> 00:10:58.834
We got all -- We got all
the major demographics.

00:10:58.834 --> 00:11:00.334
NBC is gonna be so happy

00:11:00.334 --> 00:11:01.801
when they find out
this show exists.

00:11:01.801 --> 00:11:04.033
Wait, what's that?

00:11:04.033 --> 00:11:06.701
The MAGA movement and
their leading propaganda network

00:11:06.701 --> 00:11:08.167
are in a state of panic
and disarray

00:11:08.167 --> 00:11:09.501
because they keep losing.

00:11:09.501 --> 00:11:11.300
Their political project
has been a disaster,

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:12.934
and now they're facing
a series of electoral,

00:11:12.934 --> 00:11:14.801
financial,
and legal consequences.

00:11:14.801 --> 00:11:16.734
Their top-rated host
just got axed.

00:11:16.734 --> 00:11:18.801
Their current front-runner
is under criminal indictment,

00:11:18.801 --> 00:11:20.167
and their next best hope
is a guy

00:11:20.167 --> 00:11:21.434
who looks like he just saw...

00:11:21.434 --> 00:11:24.167
-...Martians peeing
on prostitutes.

00:11:24.167 --> 00:11:26.968
[ Laughter ]

00:11:26.968 --> 00:11:29.634
Audio callback.

00:11:29.634 --> 00:11:30.968
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:30.968 --> 00:11:33.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:35.701 --> 00:11:38.234
Hey, everybody, I just want
to take a quick moment

00:11:38.234 --> 00:11:41.334
to say that there's currently
a negotiation going on

00:11:41.334 --> 00:11:43.901
with the Writers Guild
of America and the studios.

00:11:43.901 --> 00:11:46.667
A strike might happen
as of late tonight,

00:11:46.667 --> 00:11:49.734
which means this show
will be interrupted

00:11:49.734 --> 00:11:52.501
and we won't be here
to spend time with you.

00:11:52.501 --> 00:11:54.534
I want to say how grateful I am

00:11:54.534 --> 00:11:57.200
that both sides are sitting down
at the table right now

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:58.701
and that they're negotiating.

00:11:58.701 --> 00:12:01.934
And I'm hopeful that they will
be able to come to an agreement.

00:12:01.934 --> 00:12:05.434
This is a show that is built
on strong writing.

00:12:05.434 --> 00:12:07.200
Strong writing
is essential to this show.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:10.300
It's essential to any show
where the host, myself,

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:13.400
is at best a C-plus performer.

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:16.667
Really got to have the jokes.

00:12:16.667 --> 00:12:19.534
I love writing.
I love writing for TV.

00:12:19.534 --> 00:12:21.067
I love writing this show.

00:12:21.067 --> 00:12:23.033
I love that we get to
come in with an idea

00:12:23.033 --> 00:12:24.501
for what we want to do every day

00:12:24.501 --> 00:12:26.701
and we get to work
on it all afternoon.

00:12:26.701 --> 00:12:29.467
And then I have the pleasure
of coming out here

00:12:29.467 --> 00:12:32.701
and saying those words to you.

00:12:32.701 --> 00:12:34.334
No one --
Look, no one is entitled

00:12:34.334 --> 00:12:35.834
to a job in show business,

00:12:35.834 --> 00:12:38.734
but for those people
who have a job in show business,

00:12:38.734 --> 00:12:42.567
they are entitled
to fair compensation.

00:12:42.567 --> 00:12:44.367
They are entitled
to make a living.

00:12:44.367 --> 00:12:46.434
I think it's
a very reasonable demand

00:12:46.434 --> 00:12:48.300
that is being set out
by the guild,

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:49.634
and I support those demands.

00:12:49.634 --> 00:12:50.734
But I also believe

00:12:50.734 --> 00:12:52.634
that everybody at the table
right now,

00:12:52.634 --> 00:12:54.734
be it from the writers' side
or the studio side,

00:12:54.734 --> 00:12:56.901
knows that the future
of this business

00:12:56.901 --> 00:13:00.367
is dependent on storytellers.

00:13:00.367 --> 00:13:02.634
And so I'm optimistic
and hopeful

00:13:02.634 --> 00:13:05.334
that because everyone
at the table believes that,

00:13:05.334 --> 00:13:07.033
they're going to
hammer out a deal

00:13:07.033 --> 00:13:09.467
and that I can be here
with you tomorrow.

00:13:09.467 --> 00:13:12.367
Because I promise, there is
no place in the world

00:13:12.367 --> 00:13:15.000
that I would rather be.

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.968
And I'm gonna be here
the rest of the night.

00:13:16.968 --> 00:13:18.801
We'll be right back
with Chance the Rapper.

